\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/marketplace/dev-board\",\"category\":\"Marketplace\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"8\":{\"title\":\"Resources\",\"content\":\"# Resources\\n\\nCurated learning resources, tools, and guides for developers\\n\\n## Programming Languages\\n\\nLearn popular programming languages with curated resources\\n\\n[\\n\\n### JavaScript\\n\\nWeb development essentials\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/resources/languages/javascript)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Python\\n\\nData science & automation\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/resources/languages/python)\\n\\n## General Resources\\n\\nProductivity tips and recommended tools\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Vibe Coding\\n\\nFlow state & productivity\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/resources/guides/vibe-coding)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Cyber Security\\n\\nSecurity best practices\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/resources/guides/cyber-security)\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\nEssential resources for learning programming\\n\\n[\\n\\nRoadmap.sh\\n\\nInteractive roadmaps for all developer paths\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://roadmap.sh/)[\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp\\n\\nFree courses for Python, JavaScript, HTML, CSS and more\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/)[\\n\\nCodecademy\\n\\nInteractive courses for Python, JavaScript, Java, SQL, C++ and more\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/catalog)[\\n\\nDon't Ask to Ask\\n\\nLearn how to ask questions properly in tech communities\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://dontasktoask.com/)[\\n\\nQuickType\\n\\nConvert JSON to TypeScript, Python, Go, and more\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://app.quicktype.io/)\\n\\n## Free AI Assistants\\n\\nAI tools to help you learn and code faster\\n\\n[Claude](https://claude.ai/)[Grok](https://grok.com/)[Gemini](https://gemini.google.com/)[ChatGPT](https://chatgpt.com/)\\n\\n## Code Like a Pro\\n\\nFree resources for learning different languages and technologies\\n\\n![Code Like a Pro - Free learning resources](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fresources%2Fcode-like-a-pro.png&w=828&q=75)\\n\\n[HTMLW3Schools.com](https://w3schools.com/)[CSSCodecademy.com](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[JavaScriptfreecodecamp.org](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[Reactreact.dev](https://react.dev/)[Pythonlearnpython.org](https://learnpython.org/)[Javasololearn.com](https://www.sololearn.com/)[PHPphp.net](https://www.php.net/manual/en/tutorial.php)[Cybersecuritytryhackme.com](https://tryhackme.com/)[Clearn-c.org](https://learn-c.org/)[C++learncpp.com](https://www.learncpp.com/)[AWSskillbuilder.aws](https://skillbuilder.aws/)[AI / MLcoursera.org](https://www.coursera.org/)[Gitlearngitbranching.js.org](https://learngitbranching.js.org/)[SQLsqlbolt.com](https://sqlbolt.com/)\\n\\n## Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools and services\\n\\n[\\n\\nServerHunter\\n\\nFind cheap VPS and server deals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.serverhunter.com/)[\\n\\nMAS Genuine ISO\\n\\nGenuine Windows installation media\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://massgrave.dev/genuine-installation-media)\\n\\n## Discord Text Formatting\\n\\nLearn how to format your messages in Discord\\n\\n![Discord text formatting guide](/images/resources/discord-text-formating.gif)\",\"description\":\"Curated learning resources, tools, and guides for developers\",\"url\":\"/resources\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"9\":{\"title\":\"JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\",\"content\":\"# JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\\n\\n## Why JavaScript?\\n\\nJavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop software.\\n\\n## Web Dev Speedrun\\n\\nThis is the exact path I took to learn web development. Follow these resources in order to build a good foundation in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Each resource builds on the previous one.\\n\\n[\\n\\n1Responsive Web Design\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - HTML & CSS fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n2Learn HTML\\n\\nCodecademy - Deep dive into HTML\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-html)[\\n\\n3Learn CSS\\n\\nCodecademy - Master CSS styling\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[\\n\\n4Responsive Web Design (2022)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Updated HTML & CSS curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n5JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Core JavaScript concepts\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[\\n\\n6Introduction to JavaScript\\n\\nCodecademy - JavaScript fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/introduction-to-javascript)[\\n\\n7JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures (v8)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Latest JavaScript curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures-v8/)\\n\\n## Node.js\\n\\nNode.js lets you run JavaScript on the server, making you a true full-stack developer. With Node.js, you can build APIs, handle databases, and create complete web applications using the same language you learned for the frontend. Download it from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/en/download).\\n\\n## React\\n\\nOnce you've learned the basics and Node.js, it's time to master React. React is the most popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces and is used by companies like Meta, Netflix, and Airbnb.\\n\\n[\\n\\nReact Official Docs\\n\\nThe best place to learn React from scratch\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://react.dev/learn)[\\n\\nReact Tutorial for Beginners\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Comprehensive React course\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/learn-react-course/)\\n\\n## Designing with shadcn/ui\\n\\n[shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) is a collection of beautifully designed, accessible components that you can copy and paste into your apps. It's built on top of Radix UI and Tailwind CSS, giving you full control over your components.\\n\\n### Component Libraries & Blocks\\n\\nThese libraries provide pre-built components and blocks that work seamlessly with shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn\\n\\nCurated list of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shadcn.io/awesome)[\\n\\nOrigin UI\\n\\nBeautiful UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://originui.com/)[\\n\\nAnimate UI\\n\\nAnimated components for React\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://animate-ui.com/)[\\n\\nMVP Blocks\\n\\nReady-to-use blocks for MVPs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://blocks.mvp-subha.me/)[\\n\\nSHSF UI\\n\\nModern component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shsfui.com/)[\\n\\nKibo UI\\n\\nAccessible component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.kibo-ui.com/)[\\n\\nReact Bits\\n\\nUseful React components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://reactbits.dev/)[\\n\\nSkiper UI\\n\\nUI components collection\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://skiper-ui.com/)[\\n\\nAceternity UI\\n\\nBeautiful animated components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://ui.aceternity.com/)[\\n\\nMagic UI\\n\\nMagical UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://magicui.design/)[\\n\\nCult UI\\n\\nModern design system\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cult-ui.com/)\\n\\n### Tools & Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools for customizing and extending shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTweakCN\\n\\nCustomize shadcn themes visually\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tweakcn.com/)[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn/ui\\n\\nGitHub collection of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/birobirobiro/awesome-shadcn-ui)\",\"description\":\"JavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop...\",\"url\":\"/resources/languages/javascript\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"10\":{\"title\":\"Python\",\"content\":\"# Python\\n\\nPython is really only relevant for specific fields like data science, machine learning, scientific computing, and automation scripting. Outside of these areas, it's not particularly useful.\\n\\nMany people choose Python as their first language because they think it's simple. While the syntax is readable, this simplicity doesn't transfer well to other languages or real-world development. If you want to become a full-stack developer, JavaScript is a much better choice since it works on both frontend and backend.\\n\\nBut if you really want to learn Python, check out [FreeCodeCamp's Scientific Computing with Python](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/scientific-computing-with-python/) or [Codecademy's Python courses](https://www.codecademy.com/catalog/language/python).\",\"description\":\"Python is really only relevant for specific fields like data science, machine learning, scientific computing, and automation scripting. Outside of these areas, it's not particularly useful.\",\"url\":\"/resources/languages/python\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"11\":{\"title\":\"Vibe Coding\",\"content\":\"# Vibe Coding\\n\\n## What is Vibe Coding?\\n\\nVibe coding is a new approach to programming where you describe what you want in natural language and let AI build it for you. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you guide the AI with prompts and let it handle the implementation.\\n\\nThe term was coined by Andrej Karpathy in this tweet:\\n\\nTo vibe code effectively, you need the right tools. Here are the best AI-powered editors and CLIs available today.\\n\\n## Choosing the Best Model\\n\\nThe AI model you use matters just as much as the tool. You can find the latest rankings of AI models for web development on the [LM Arena Web Development Leaderboard](https://lmarena.ai/leaderboard/webdev).\\n\\nThat said, Claude models by Anthropic consistently rank at the top for coding tasks. If you want the best results for vibe coding, Claude is usually the way to go.\\n\\n## My Setup\\n\\nI personally use the [Claude Code VSCode Extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=anthropics.claude-code) for my vibe coding workflow. It integrates Claude directly into VSCode with agentic capabilities.\\n\\nTo help gather context for AI assistants, I also built the [Code Collector](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=0-don.code-collector) extension. It automatically collects files based on import dependencies, making it easy to provide your codebase context to any AI assistant.\\n\\n## AI Editors\\n\\nThese editors have AI deeply integrated into the coding experience, allowing you to chat with AI, generate code, and get intelligent completions.\\n\\n[\\n\\nCursor\\n\\nAI-first code editor built on VSCode\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cursor.com/)[\\n\\nWindsurf\\n\\nAI-powered IDE by Codeium\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://codeium.com/windsurf)[\\n\\nAntigravity\\n\\nAI coding environment\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://antigravity.google/)\\n\\n## AI CLIs\\n\\nCommand-line tools that let you vibe code directly from your terminal. These are great for quick tasks, automation, and working in any editor you prefer.\\n\\n[\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\nAnthropic's agentic coding CLI\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code)[\\n\\nOpenAI Codex CLI\\n\\nOpenAI's terminal coding assistant\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/openai/codex)[\\n\\nGemini CLI\\n\\nGoogle's AI coding assistant for terminal\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli)\",\"description\":\"Vibe coding is a new approach to programming where you describe what you want in natural language and let AI build it for you. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you guide the AI with pro...\",\"url\":\"/resources/guides/vibe-coding\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"12\":{\"title\":\"Cyber Security\",\"content\":\"# Cyber Security\\n\\n## Introduction\\n\\nLet's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then reality hit: turns out hacking is mostly just... coding. A lot of coding.\\n\\nBut that's actually the good news. The skills you learn in cyber security - understanding systems, networks, and how software works - make you a better developer overall. Whether you end up in pentesting, security engineering, or just writing more secure code, it all starts with the fundamentals.\\n\\n## Learning Platforms\\n\\nThe best way to learn cyber security is by doing. These platforms offer hands-on challenges, CTFs, and virtual labs where you can practice legally and safely.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTryHackMe\\n\\nFree online platform for learning cyber security with hands-on exercises and labs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tryhackme.com/)[\\n\\nHack The Box\\n\\nCyber mastery platform with beginner-friendly modules and real-world challenges\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://hackthebox.com/)[\\n\\npicoCTF\\n\\nFree computer security education program by Carnegie Mellon University\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.picoctf.org/)[\\n\\nRoot Me\\n\\nPlatform for practicing hacking skills with challenges and virtual environments\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.root-me.org/)[\\n\\nCisco Networking Academy\\n\\nLearn cybersecurity, networking, and Python from Cisco's official training program\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://netacad.com/)\",\"description\":\"Let's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then re...\",\"url\":\"/resources/guides/cyber-security\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"13\":{\"title\":\"JavaScript\",\"content\":\"# JavaScript(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/javascript\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"14\":{\"title\":\"Python\",\"content\":\"# Python(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/python\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"15\":{\"title\":\"Rust\",\"content\":\"# Rust(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/rust\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"16\":{\"title\":\"C++\",\"content\":\"# C++(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/cpp\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"17\":{\"title\":\"C#\",\"content\":\"# C#(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/csharp\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"18\":{\"title\":\"C\",\"content\":\"# C(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/c\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"19\":{\"title\":\"Go\",\"content\":\"# Go(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/go\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"20\":{\"title\":\"Java\",\"content\":\"# Java(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/java\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"21\":{\"title\":\"Kotlin\",\"content\":\"# Kotlin(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/kotlin\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"22\":{\"title\":\"Dart\",\"content\":\"# Dart(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/dart\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"23\":{\"title\":\"Lua\",\"content\":\"# Lua(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/lua\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"24\":{\"title\":\"PHP\",\"content\":\"# PHP(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/php\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"25\":{\"title\":\"HTML/CSS\",\"content\":\"# HTML/CSS(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/html-css\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"26\":{\"title\":\"SQL\",\"content\":\"# SQL(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/sql\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"27\":{\"title\":\"Swift\",\"content\":\"# Swift(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/swift\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"28\":{\"title\":\"Bash/PowerShell\",\"content\":\"# Bash/PowerShell(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/bash-powershell\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"29\":{\"title\":\"Visual Basic\",\"content\":\"# Visual Basic(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/visual-basic\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"30\":{\"title\":\"Zig\",\"content\":\"# Zig(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/zig\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"31\":{\"title\":\"Other Languages\",\"content\":\"# Other Languages(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/other\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"32\":{\"title\":\"Neueste Nachrichten\",\"content\":\"# Neueste Nachrichten\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/news\",\"category\":\"Community\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"33\":{\"title\":\"Community-Richtlinien\",\"content\":\"# Community-Richtlinien\\n\\n\\\\>catcommunity\\\\_rules.txt\\n\\n12 Regeln erfolgreich geladen...\\n\\n#1Allgemein\\n\\n### 1\\\\. Discord-Richtlinien\\n\\nDie Discord-Community-Richtlinien gelten für Programming \\\\[DE / EN\\\\]; Benutzer können diese unter https://discord.com/guidelines einsehen.\\n\\n#2Allgemein\\n\\n### 2\\\\. Sprache\\n\\nDie Sprache unserer Community ist Deutsch und Englisch. Im Voice-Channel \\\"Public \\\\[DE\\\\]\\\" ist Deutsch die Hauptsprache. Benutzer können freiwillig Englisch sprechen. Im Voice-Channel \\\"Public \\\\[EN\\\\]\\\" müssen Benutzer jedoch Englisch sprechen.\\n\\n#3Allgemein\\n\\n### 3\\\\. Fragen stellen\\n\\n3.1 Niemand ist verpflichtet zu helfen oder eine Frage zu beantworten. Hilfe ist grundsätzlich kostenlos. 3.2 Mitglieder mit der Rolle \\\"HELPER\\\" haben sich freiwillig bereit erklärt, bei Fragen zu helfen. 3.3 Das Anpingen von Mitgliedern, um eine schnellere Antwort zu erwarten, ist nicht erlaubt. 3.4 Stellen Sie keine Fragen wie \\\"Kennt sich jemand mit XY aus?\\\", sondern stellen Sie die Frage direkt, siehe auch ➔ https://dontasktoask.com/. 3.5 Beachten Sie den Thread \\\"Wie stelle ich eine gute Frage?\\\" auf Stackoverflow ➔ https://stackoverflow.com/help/how-to-ask.\\n\\n#4Verhalten\\n\\n### 4\\\\. Aufnahmen\\n\\nDas Aufzeichnen von Videos (Bildschirmfreigabe, Webcam) und Ton (Voice-Chat) ist auf diesem Discord nicht gestattet.\\n\\n#5Verhalten\\n\\n### 5\\\\. Werbung\\n\\nJegliche Art von Drittwerbung ist verboten.\\n\\n#6Autorität\\n\\n### 6\\\\. Moderatoren\\n\\nDas Moderationsteam hat das Recht, angemessene Maßnahmen gegen einen Benutzer zu ergreifen, auch wenn eine bestimmte Regel nicht ausdrücklich verletzt wurde.\\n\\n#7Verhalten\\n\\n### 7\\\\. Direktnachrichten\\n\\nBitte unterlassen Sie es, Direktnachrichten an die Administratoren zu senden.\\n\\n#8Verhalten\\n\\n### 8\\\\. Weitergabe persönlicher Informationen\\n\\nDie Weitergabe persönlicher Informationen anderer Personen jeglicher Art ohne deren Zustimmung ist verboten und führt zu einem permanenten Bann.\\n\\n#9Autorität\\n\\n### 9\\\\. Durchsetzung einer Maßnahme\\n\\nDie Auslegung der Regeln liegt im Ermessen des jeweiligen Administrators.\\n\\n#10Inhalt\\n\\n### 10\\\\. KI-Nutzung / Spam / Stellenangebote\\n\\nDie Verwendung von KI zur Erstellung von Stellenangeboten oder anderen Spam-Inhalten ist nicht gestattet. Benutzer, die dabei erwischt werden, werden eingesperrt, stummgeschaltet oder gebannt.\\n\\n#11Inhalt\\n\\n### 11\\\\. Gefälschte Fähigkeiten / Code-Stacks\\n\\nDas falsche Behaupten von Fähigkeiten oder Erfahrungen zum Zweck des Betrugs oder der Erlangung von Jobs ist verboten. Benutzer müssen in der Lage sein, ihre Fähigkeiten zu beweisen.\\n\\n#12Inhalt\\n\\n### 12\\\\. Keine DM\\n\\nKeine Direktnachrichten ohne vorherige Genehmigung. Wenn Sie jemand meldet, können Sie stummgeschaltet oder eingeschränkt werden.\",\"description\":\"Die Discord-Community-Richtlinien gelten für Programming [DE / EN]; Benutzer können diese unter https://discord.com/guidelines einsehen.\",\"url\":\"/community/rules\",\"category\":\"Community\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"34\":{\"title\":\"Community-Showcase\",\"content\":\"# Community-Showcase(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/showcase\",\"category\":\"Community\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"35\":{\"title\":\"Unser Team\",\"content\":\"# Unser Team\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/team\",\"category\":\"Community\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"36\":{\"title\":\"Marktplatz\",\"content\":\"# Marktplatz(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/marketplace\",\"category\":\"Marketplace\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"37\":{\"title\":\"Jobbörse\",\"content\":\"# Jobbörse(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/marketplace/job-board\",\"category\":\"Marketplace\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"38\":{\"title\":\"Entwickler-Board\",\"content\":\"# Entwickler-Board(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/marketplace/dev-board\",\"category\":\"Marketplace\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"39\":{\"title\":\"Resources\",\"content\":\"# Resources\\n\\nCurated learning resources, tools, and guides for developers\\n\\n## Programming Languages\\n\\nLearn popular programming languages with curated resources\\n\\n[\\n\\n### JavaScript\\n\\nWeb development essentials\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/ressourcen/sprachen/javascript)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Python\\n\\nData science & automation\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/ressourcen/sprachen/python)\\n\\n## General Resources\\n\\nProductivity tips and recommended tools\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Vibe Coding\\n\\nFlow state & productivity\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/ressourcen/anleitungen/vibe-coding)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Cyber Security\\n\\nSecurity best practices\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/ressourcen/anleitungen/cyber-security)\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\nEssential resources for learning programming\\n\\n[\\n\\nRoadmap.sh\\n\\nInteractive roadmaps for all developer paths\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://roadmap.sh/)[\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp\\n\\nFree courses for Python, JavaScript, HTML, CSS and more\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/)[\\n\\nCodecademy\\n\\nInteractive courses for Python, JavaScript, Java, SQL, C++ and more\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/catalog)[\\n\\nDon't Ask to Ask\\n\\nLearn how to ask questions properly in tech communities\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://dontasktoask.com/)[\\n\\nQuickType\\n\\nConvert JSON to TypeScript, Python, Go, and more\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://app.quicktype.io/)\\n\\n## Free AI Assistants\\n\\nAI tools to help you learn and code faster\\n\\n[Claude](https://claude.ai/)[Grok](https://grok.com/)[Gemini](https://gemini.google.com/)[ChatGPT](https://chatgpt.com/)\\n\\n## Code Like a Pro\\n\\nFree resources for learning different languages and technologies\\n\\n![Code Like a Pro - Free learning resources](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fresources%2Fcode-like-a-pro.png&w=828&q=75)\\n\\n[HTMLW3Schools.com](https://w3schools.com/)[CSSCodecademy.com](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[JavaScriptfreecodecamp.org](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[Reactreact.dev](https://react.dev/)[Pythonlearnpython.org](https://learnpython.org/)[Javasololearn.com](https://www.sololearn.com/)[PHPphp.net](https://www.php.net/manual/en/tutorial.php)[Cybersecuritytryhackme.com](https://tryhackme.com/)[Clearn-c.org](https://learn-c.org/)[C++learncpp.com](https://www.learncpp.com/)[AWSskillbuilder.aws](https://skillbuilder.aws/)[AI / MLcoursera.org](https://www.coursera.org/)[Gitlearngitbranching.js.org](https://learngitbranching.js.org/)[SQLsqlbolt.com](https://sqlbolt.com/)\\n\\n## Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools and services\\n\\n[\\n\\nServerHunter\\n\\nFind cheap VPS and server deals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.serverhunter.com/)[\\n\\nMAS Genuine ISO\\n\\nGenuine Windows installation media\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://massgrave.dev/genuine-installation-media)\\n\\n## Discord Text Formatting\\n\\nLearn how to format your messages in Discord\\n\\n![Discord text formatting guide](/images/resources/discord-text-formating.gif)\",\"description\":\"Curated learning resources, tools, and guides for developers\",\"url\":\"/resources\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"40\":{\"title\":\"JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\",\"content\":\"# JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\\n\\n## Why JavaScript?\\n\\nJavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop software.\\n\\n## Web Dev Speedrun\\n\\nThis is the exact path I took to learn web development. Follow these resources in order to build a good foundation in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Each resource builds on the previous one.\\n\\n[\\n\\n1Responsive Web Design\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - HTML & CSS fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n2Learn HTML\\n\\nCodecademy - Deep dive into HTML\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-html)[\\n\\n3Learn CSS\\n\\nCodecademy - Master CSS styling\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[\\n\\n4Responsive Web Design (2022)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Updated HTML & CSS curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n5JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Core JavaScript concepts\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[\\n\\n6Introduction to JavaScript\\n\\nCodecademy - JavaScript fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/introduction-to-javascript)[\\n\\n7JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures (v8)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Latest JavaScript curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures-v8/)\\n\\n## Node.js\\n\\nNode.js lets you run JavaScript on the server, making you a true full-stack developer. With Node.js, you can build APIs, handle databases, and create complete web applications using the same language you learned for the frontend. Download it from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/en/download).\\n\\n## React\\n\\nOnce you've learned the basics and Node.js, it's time to master React. React is the most popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces and is used by companies like Meta, Netflix, and Airbnb.\\n\\n[\\n\\nReact Official Docs\\n\\nThe best place to learn React from scratch\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://react.dev/learn)[\\n\\nReact Tutorial for Beginners\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Comprehensive React course\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/learn-react-course/)\\n\\n## Designing with shadcn/ui\\n\\n[shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) is a collection of beautifully designed, accessible components that you can copy and paste into your apps. It's built on top of Radix UI and Tailwind CSS, giving you full control over your components.\\n\\n### Component Libraries & Blocks\\n\\nThese libraries provide pre-built components and blocks that work seamlessly with shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn\\n\\nCurated list of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shadcn.io/awesome)[\\n\\nOrigin UI\\n\\nBeautiful UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://originui.com/)[\\n\\nAnimate UI\\n\\nAnimated components for React\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://animate-ui.com/)[\\n\\nMVP Blocks\\n\\nReady-to-use blocks for MVPs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://blocks.mvp-subha.me/)[\\n\\nSHSF UI\\n\\nModern component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shsfui.com/)[\\n\\nKibo UI\\n\\nAccessible component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.kibo-ui.com/)[\\n\\nReact Bits\\n\\nUseful React components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://reactbits.dev/)[\\n\\nSkiper UI\\n\\nUI components collection\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://skiper-ui.com/)[\\n\\nAceternity UI\\n\\nBeautiful animated components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://ui.aceternity.com/)[\\n\\nMagic UI\\n\\nMagical UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://magicui.design/)[\\n\\nCult UI\\n\\nModern design system\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cult-ui.com/)\\n\\n### Tools & Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools for customizing and extending shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTweakCN\\n\\nCustomize shadcn themes visually\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tweakcn.com/)[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn/ui\\n\\nGitHub collection of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/birobirobiro/awesome-shadcn-ui)\",\"description\":\"JavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop...\",\"url\":\"/resources/languages/javascript\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"41\":{\"title\":\"Python\",\"content\":\"# Python\\n\\nPython is really only relevant for specific fields like data science, machine learning, scientific computing, and automation scripting. Outside of these areas, it's not particularly useful.\\n\\nMany people choose Python as their first language because they think it's simple. While the syntax is readable, this simplicity doesn't transfer well to other languages or real-world development. If you want to become a full-stack developer, JavaScript is a much better choice since it works on both frontend and backend.\\n\\nBut if you really want to learn Python, check out [FreeCodeCamp's Scientific Computing with Python](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/scientific-computing-with-python/) or [Codecademy's Python courses](https://www.codecademy.com/catalog/language/python).\",\"description\":\"Python is really only relevant for specific fields like data science, machine learning, scientific computing, and automation scripting. Outside of these areas, it's not particularly useful.\",\"url\":\"/resources/languages/python\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"42\":{\"title\":\"Vibe Coding\",\"content\":\"# Vibe Coding\\n\\n## What is Vibe Coding?\\n\\nVibe coding is a new approach to programming where you describe what you want in natural language and let AI build it for you. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you guide the AI with prompts and let it handle the implementation.\\n\\nThe term was coined by Andrej Karpathy in this tweet:\\n\\nTo vibe code effectively, you need the right tools. Here are the best AI-powered editors and CLIs available today.\\n\\n## Choosing the Best Model\\n\\nThe AI model you use matters just as much as the tool. You can find the latest rankings of AI models for web development on the [LM Arena Web Development Leaderboard](https://lmarena.ai/leaderboard/webdev).\\n\\nThat said, Claude models by Anthropic consistently rank at the top for coding tasks. If you want the best results for vibe coding, Claude is usually the way to go.\\n\\n## My Setup\\n\\nI personally use the [Claude Code VSCode Extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=anthropics.claude-code) for my vibe coding workflow. It integrates Claude directly into VSCode with agentic capabilities.\\n\\nTo help gather context for AI assistants, I also built the [Code Collector](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=0-don.code-collector) extension. It automatically collects files based on import dependencies, making it easy to provide your codebase context to any AI assistant.\\n\\n## AI Editors\\n\\nThese editors have AI deeply integrated into the coding experience, allowing you to chat with AI, generate code, and get intelligent completions.\\n\\n[\\n\\nCursor\\n\\nAI-first code editor built on VSCode\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cursor.com/)[\\n\\nWindsurf\\n\\nAI-powered IDE by Codeium\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://codeium.com/windsurf)[\\n\\nAntigravity\\n\\nAI coding environment\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://antigravity.google/)\\n\\n## AI CLIs\\n\\nCommand-line tools that let you vibe code directly from your terminal. These are great for quick tasks, automation, and working in any editor you prefer.\\n\\n[\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\nAnthropic's agentic coding CLI\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code)[\\n\\nOpenAI Codex CLI\\n\\nOpenAI's terminal coding assistant\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/openai/codex)[\\n\\nGemini CLI\\n\\nGoogle's AI coding assistant for terminal\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli)\",\"description\":\"Vibe coding is a new approach to programming where you describe what you want in natural language and let AI build it for you. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you guide the AI with pro...\",\"url\":\"/resources/guides/vibe-coding\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"43\":{\"title\":\"Cyber Security\",\"content\":\"# Cyber Security\\n\\n## Introduction\\n\\nLet's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then reality hit: turns out hacking is mostly just... coding. A lot of coding.\\n\\nBut that's actually the good news. The skills you learn in cyber security - understanding systems, networks, and how software works - make you a better developer overall. Whether you end up in pentesting, security engineering, or just writing more secure code, it all starts with the fundamentals.\\n\\n## Learning Platforms\\n\\nThe best way to learn cyber security is by doing. These platforms offer hands-on challenges, CTFs, and virtual labs where you can practice legally and safely.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTryHackMe\\n\\nFree online platform for learning cyber security with hands-on exercises and labs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tryhackme.com/)[\\n\\nHack The Box\\n\\nCyber mastery platform with beginner-friendly modules and real-world challenges\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://hackthebox.com/)[\\n\\npicoCTF\\n\\nFree computer security education program by Carnegie Mellon University\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.picoctf.org/)[\\n\\nRoot Me\\n\\nPlatform for practicing hacking skills with challenges and virtual environments\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.root-me.org/)[\\n\\nCisco Networking Academy\\n\\nLearn cybersecurity, networking, and Python from Cisco's official training program\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://netacad.com/)\",\"description\":\"Let's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then re...\",\"url\":\"/resources/guides/cyber-security\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"44\":{\"title\":\"JavaScript\",\"content\":\"# JavaScript(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/javascript\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"45\":{\"title\":\"Python\",\"content\":\"# Python(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/python\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"46\":{\"title\":\"Rust\",\"content\":\"# Rust(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/rust\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"47\":{\"title\":\"C++\",\"content\":\"# C++(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/cpp\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"48\":{\"title\":\"C#\",\"content\":\"# C#(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/csharp\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"49\":{\"title\":\"C\",\"content\":\"# C(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/c\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"50\":{\"title\":\"Go\",\"content\":\"# Go(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/go\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"51\":{\"title\":\"Java\",\"content\":\"# Java(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/java\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"52\":{\"title\":\"Kotlin\",\"content\":\"# Kotlin(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/kotlin\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"53\":{\"title\":\"Dart\",\"content\":\"# Dart(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/dart\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"54\":{\"title\":\"Lua\",\"content\":\"# Lua(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/lua\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"55\":{\"title\":\"PHP\",\"content\":\"# PHP(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/php\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"56\":{\"title\":\"HTML/CSS\",\"content\":\"# HTML/CSS(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/html-css\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"57\":{\"title\":\"SQL\",\"content\":\"# SQL(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/sql\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"58\":{\"title\":\"Swift\",\"content\":\"# Swift(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/swift\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"59\":{\"title\":\"Bash/PowerShell\",\"content\":\"# Bash/PowerShell(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/bash-powershell\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"60\":{\"title\":\"Visual Basic\",\"content\":\"# Visual Basic(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/visual-basic\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"61\":{\"title\":\"Zig\",\"content\":\"# Zig(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/zig\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"},\"62\":{\"title\":\"Andere Sprachen\",\"content\":\"# Andere Sprachen(0)\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"/community/coding/other\",\"category\":\"Coding\",\"locale\":\"de\"}},\"count\":62},\"sorting\":{\"language\":\"english\",\"sortableProperties\":[\"title\",\"content\",\"description\",\"url\"],\"sortablePropertiesWithTypes\":{\"title\":\"string\",\"content\":\"string\",\"description\":\"string\",\"url\":\"string\"},\"sorts\":{\"title\":{\"docs\":{\"1\":33,\"2\":9,\"3\":10,\"4\":40,\"5\":36,\"6\":29,\"7\":17,\"8\":47,\"9\":27,\"10\":43,\"11\":56,\"12\":13,\"13\":25,\"14\":44,\"15\":49,\"16\":7,\"17\":5,\"18\":3,\"19\":19,\"20\":23,\"21\":31,\"22\":15,\"23\":34,\"24\":41,\"25\":21,\"26\":51,\"27\":53,\"28\":1,\"29\":58,\"30\":60,\"31\":39,\"32\":38,\"33\":11,\"34\":12,\"35\":55,\"36\":37,\"37\":30,\"38\":18,\"39\":48,\"40\":28,\"41\":45,\"42\":57,\"43\":14,\"44\":26,\"45\":46,\"46\":50,\"47\":8,\"48\":6,\"49\":4,\"50\":20,\"51\":24,\"52\":32,\"53\":16,\"54\":35,\"55\":42,\"56\":22,\"57\":52,\"58\":54,\"59\":2,\"60\":59,\"61\":61,\"62\":0},\"orderedDocs\":[[62,\"Andere Sprachen\"],[28,\"Bash/PowerShell\"],[59,\"Bash/PowerShell\"],[18,\"C\"],[49,\"C\"],[17,\"C#\"],[48,\"C#\"],[16,\"C++\"],[47,\"C++\"],[2,\"Community Guidelines\"],[3,\"Community Showcase\"],[33,\"Community-Richtlinien\"],[34,\"Community-Showcase\"],[12,\"Cyber Security\"],[43,\"Cyber Security\"],[22,\"Dart\"],[53,\"Dart\"],[7,\"Developer Board\"],[38,\"Entwickler-Board\"],[19,\"Go\"],[50,\"Go\"],[25,\"HTML/CSS\"],[56,\"HTML/CSS\"],[20,\"Java\"],[51,\"Java\"],[13,\"JavaScript\"],[44,\"JavaScript\"],[9,\"JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\"],[40,\"JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\"],[6,\"Job Board\"],[37,\"Jobbörse\"],[21,\"Kotlin\"],[52,\"Kotlin\"],[1,\"Latest News\"],[23,\"Lua\"],[54,\"Lua\"],[5,\"Marketplace\"],[36,\"Marktplatz\"],[32,\"Neueste Nachrichten\"],[31,\"Other Languages\"],[4,\"Our Team\"],[24,\"PHP\"],[55,\"PHP\"],[10,\"Python\"],[14,\"Python\"],[41,\"Python\"],[45,\"Python\"],[8,\"Resources\"],[39,\"Resources\"],[15,\"Rust\"],[46,\"Rust\"],[26,\"SQL\"],[57,\"SQL\"],[27,\"Swift\"],[58,\"Swift\"],[35,\"Unser Team\"],[11,\"Vibe Coding\"],[42,\"Vibe Coding\"],[29,\"Visual Basic\"],[60,\"Visual Basic\"],[30,\"Zig\"],[61,\"Zig\"]],\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"docs\":{\"1\":33,\"2\":9,\"3\":10,\"4\":40,\"5\":36,\"6\":29,\"7\":17,\"8\":48,\"9\":25,\"10\":43,\"11\":56,\"12\":13,\"13\":27,\"14\":45,\"15\":49,\"16\":7,\"17\":5,\"18\":3,\"19\":19,\"20\":23,\"21\":31,\"22\":15,\"23\":34,\"24\":41,\"25\":21,\"26\":51,\"27\":53,\"28\":1,\"29\":58,\"30\":60,\"31\":39,\"32\":38,\"33\":11,\"34\":12,\"35\":55,\"36\":37,\"37\":30,\"38\":18,\"39\":47,\"40\":26,\"41\":44,\"42\":57,\"43\":14,\"44\":28,\"45\":46,\"46\":50,\"47\":8,\"48\":6,\"49\":4,\"50\":20,\"51\":24,\"52\":32,\"53\":16,\"54\":35,\"55\":42,\"56\":22,\"57\":52,\"58\":54,\"59\":2,\"60\":59,\"61\":61,\"62\":0},\"orderedDocs\":[[62,\"# Andere Sprachen(0)\"],[28,\"# Bash/PowerShell(0)\"],[59,\"# Bash/PowerShell(0)\"],[18,\"# C(0)\"],[49,\"# C(0)\"],[17,\"# C#(0)\"],[48,\"# C#(0)\"],[16,\"# C++(0)\"],[47,\"# C++(0)\"],[2,\"# Community Guidelines\\n\\n\\\\>catcommunity\\\\_rules.txt\\n\\n12 rules loaded successfully...\\n\\n#1General\\n\\n### 1\\\\. Discord guidelines\\n\\nThe Discord Community Guidelines apply to Programming \\\\[DE / EN\\\\]; users can view these at https://discord.com/guidelines.\\n\\n#2General\\n\\n### 2\\\\. Language\\n\\nThe language of our community is German and English. In the voice channel, \\\"Public \\\\[DE\\\\]\\\" German is the primary language. Users can speak English voluntarily. However, users must speak English in the Voice Channel \\\"Public \\\\[EN\\\\]\\\".\\n\\n#3General\\n\\n### 3\\\\. Asking questions\\n\\n3.1 Nobody is obliged to help or answer a question. Help is generally free of charge. 3.2 Members with the role of \\\"HELPER\\\" have volunteered to help with questions. 3.3 Pinging members to expect a faster response is not allowed. 3.4 Don't ask questions like \\\"Does anyone know about XY?\\\" ask the question directly, see also ➔ https://dontasktoask.com/. 3.5 Note the thread \\\"How do I ask a good question?\\\" on Stackoverflow ➔ https://stackoverflow.com/help/how-to-ask.\\n\\n#4Behavior\\n\\n### 4\\\\. Recording\\n\\nThe recording of videos (screen sharing, webcam) and sound (voice chat) is not permitted on this Discord.\\n\\n#5Behavior\\n\\n### 5\\\\. Advertising\\n\\nAny kind of third-party advertising is prohibited.\\n\\n#6Authority\\n\\n### 6\\\\. Moderators\\n\\nThe moderation team has the right to take appropriate actions against a user, even if a certain rule has not been explicitly violated.\\n\\n#7Behavior\\n\\n### 7\\\\. Direct messages\\n\\nPlease refrain from sending direct messages to the administrators.\\n\\n#8Behavior\\n\\n### 8\\\\. Dissemination of personal information\\n\\nDissemination of other people's personal information of any kind without their consent is prohibited and will result in a permanent ban.\\n\\n#9Authority\\n\\n### 9\\\\. Enforcement of a measure\\n\\nThe interpretation of the rules is at the discretion of the respective administrator.\\n\\n#10Content\\n\\n### 10\\\\. AI Use / Spam / Job listings\\n\\nThe use of AI to make job listings or other spam content is not permitted. Users found doing so will be jailed, muted, or banned.\\n\\n#11Content\\n\\n### 11\\\\. Fake Skills / Code Stacks\\n\\nFalsely claiming to have skills or experience for the purpose of scamming or obtaining jobs is prohibited. Users must be able to prove their skills.\\n\\n#12Content\\n\\n### 12\\\\. No DM\\n\\nNo direct messages without previous authorization. If someone reports you, you may be muted or restricted.\"],[3,\"# Community Showcase(0)\"],[33,\"# Community-Richtlinien\\n\\n\\\\>catcommunity\\\\_rules.txt\\n\\n12 Regeln erfolgreich geladen...\\n\\n#1Allgemein\\n\\n### 1\\\\. Discord-Richtlinien\\n\\nDie Discord-Community-Richtlinien gelten für Programming \\\\[DE / EN\\\\]; Benutzer können diese unter https://discord.com/guidelines einsehen.\\n\\n#2Allgemein\\n\\n### 2\\\\. Sprache\\n\\nDie Sprache unserer Community ist Deutsch und Englisch. Im Voice-Channel \\\"Public \\\\[DE\\\\]\\\" ist Deutsch die Hauptsprache. Benutzer können freiwillig Englisch sprechen. Im Voice-Channel \\\"Public \\\\[EN\\\\]\\\" müssen Benutzer jedoch Englisch sprechen.\\n\\n#3Allgemein\\n\\n### 3\\\\. Fragen stellen\\n\\n3.1 Niemand ist verpflichtet zu helfen oder eine Frage zu beantworten. Hilfe ist grundsätzlich kostenlos. 3.2 Mitglieder mit der Rolle \\\"HELPER\\\" haben sich freiwillig bereit erklärt, bei Fragen zu helfen. 3.3 Das Anpingen von Mitgliedern, um eine schnellere Antwort zu erwarten, ist nicht erlaubt. 3.4 Stellen Sie keine Fragen wie \\\"Kennt sich jemand mit XY aus?\\\", sondern stellen Sie die Frage direkt, siehe auch ➔ https://dontasktoask.com/. 3.5 Beachten Sie den Thread \\\"Wie stelle ich eine gute Frage?\\\" auf Stackoverflow ➔ https://stackoverflow.com/help/how-to-ask.\\n\\n#4Verhalten\\n\\n### 4\\\\. Aufnahmen\\n\\nDas Aufzeichnen von Videos (Bildschirmfreigabe, Webcam) und Ton (Voice-Chat) ist auf diesem Discord nicht gestattet.\\n\\n#5Verhalten\\n\\n### 5\\\\. Werbung\\n\\nJegliche Art von Drittwerbung ist verboten.\\n\\n#6Autorität\\n\\n### 6\\\\. Moderatoren\\n\\nDas Moderationsteam hat das Recht, angemessene Maßnahmen gegen einen Benutzer zu ergreifen, auch wenn eine bestimmte Regel nicht ausdrücklich verletzt wurde.\\n\\n#7Verhalten\\n\\n### 7\\\\. Direktnachrichten\\n\\nBitte unterlassen Sie es, Direktnachrichten an die Administratoren zu senden.\\n\\n#8Verhalten\\n\\n### 8\\\\. Weitergabe persönlicher Informationen\\n\\nDie Weitergabe persönlicher Informationen anderer Personen jeglicher Art ohne deren Zustimmung ist verboten und führt zu einem permanenten Bann.\\n\\n#9Autorität\\n\\n### 9\\\\. Durchsetzung einer Maßnahme\\n\\nDie Auslegung der Regeln liegt im Ermessen des jeweiligen Administrators.\\n\\n#10Inhalt\\n\\n### 10\\\\. KI-Nutzung / Spam / Stellenangebote\\n\\nDie Verwendung von KI zur Erstellung von Stellenangeboten oder anderen Spam-Inhalten ist nicht gestattet. Benutzer, die dabei erwischt werden, werden eingesperrt, stummgeschaltet oder gebannt.\\n\\n#11Inhalt\\n\\n### 11\\\\. Gefälschte Fähigkeiten / Code-Stacks\\n\\nDas falsche Behaupten von Fähigkeiten oder Erfahrungen zum Zweck des Betrugs oder der Erlangung von Jobs ist verboten. Benutzer müssen in der Lage sein, ihre Fähigkeiten zu beweisen.\\n\\n#12Inhalt\\n\\n### 12\\\\. Keine DM\\n\\nKeine Direktnachrichten ohne vorherige Genehmigung. Wenn Sie jemand meldet, können Sie stummgeschaltet oder eingeschränkt werden.\"],[34,\"# Community-Showcase(0)\"],[12,\"# Cyber Security\\n\\n## Introduction\\n\\nLet's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then reality hit: turns out hacking is mostly just... coding. A lot of coding.\\n\\nBut that's actually the good news. The skills you learn in cyber security - understanding systems, networks, and how software works - make you a better developer overall. Whether you end up in pentesting, security engineering, or just writing more secure code, it all starts with the fundamentals.\\n\\n## Learning Platforms\\n\\nThe best way to learn cyber security is by doing. These platforms offer hands-on challenges, CTFs, and virtual labs where you can practice legally and safely.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTryHackMe\\n\\nFree online platform for learning cyber security with hands-on exercises and labs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tryhackme.com/)[\\n\\nHack The Box\\n\\nCyber mastery platform with beginner-friendly modules and real-world challenges\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://hackthebox.com/)[\\n\\npicoCTF\\n\\nFree computer security education program by Carnegie Mellon University\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.picoctf.org/)[\\n\\nRoot Me\\n\\nPlatform for practicing hacking skills with challenges and virtual environments\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.root-me.org/)[\\n\\nCisco Networking Academy\\n\\nLearn cybersecurity, networking, and Python from Cisco's official training program\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://netacad.com/)\"],[43,\"# Cyber Security\\n\\n## Introduction\\n\\nLet's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then reality hit: turns out hacking is mostly just... coding. A lot of coding.\\n\\nBut that's actually the good news. The skills you learn in cyber security - understanding systems, networks, and how software works - make you a better developer overall. Whether you end up in pentesting, security engineering, or just writing more secure code, it all starts with the fundamentals.\\n\\n## Learning Platforms\\n\\nThe best way to learn cyber security is by doing. These platforms offer hands-on challenges, CTFs, and virtual labs where you can practice legally and safely.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTryHackMe\\n\\nFree online platform for learning cyber security with hands-on exercises and labs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tryhackme.com/)[\\n\\nHack The Box\\n\\nCyber mastery platform with beginner-friendly modules and real-world challenges\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://hackthebox.com/)[\\n\\npicoCTF\\n\\nFree computer security education program by Carnegie Mellon University\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.picoctf.org/)[\\n\\nRoot Me\\n\\nPlatform for practicing hacking skills with challenges and virtual environments\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.root-me.org/)[\\n\\nCisco Networking Academy\\n\\nLearn cybersecurity, networking, and Python from Cisco's official training program\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://netacad.com/)\"],[22,\"# Dart(0)\"],[53,\"# Dart(0)\"],[7,\"# Developer Board(0)\"],[38,\"# Entwickler-Board(0)\"],[19,\"# Go(0)\"],[50,\"# Go(0)\"],[25,\"# HTML/CSS(0)\"],[56,\"# HTML/CSS(0)\"],[20,\"# Java(0)\"],[51,\"# Java(0)\"],[9,\"# JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\\n\\n## Why JavaScript?\\n\\nJavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop software.\\n\\n## Web Dev Speedrun\\n\\nThis is the exact path I took to learn web development. Follow these resources in order to build a good foundation in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Each resource builds on the previous one.\\n\\n[\\n\\n1Responsive Web Design\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - HTML & CSS fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n2Learn HTML\\n\\nCodecademy - Deep dive into HTML\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-html)[\\n\\n3Learn CSS\\n\\nCodecademy - Master CSS styling\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[\\n\\n4Responsive Web Design (2022)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Updated HTML & CSS curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n5JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Core JavaScript concepts\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[\\n\\n6Introduction to JavaScript\\n\\nCodecademy - JavaScript fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/introduction-to-javascript)[\\n\\n7JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures (v8)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Latest JavaScript curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures-v8/)\\n\\n## Node.js\\n\\nNode.js lets you run JavaScript on the server, making you a true full-stack developer. With Node.js, you can build APIs, handle databases, and create complete web applications using the same language you learned for the frontend. Download it from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/en/download).\\n\\n## React\\n\\nOnce you've learned the basics and Node.js, it's time to master React. React is the most popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces and is used by companies like Meta, Netflix, and Airbnb.\\n\\n[\\n\\nReact Official Docs\\n\\nThe best place to learn React from scratch\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://react.dev/learn)[\\n\\nReact Tutorial for Beginners\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Comprehensive React course\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/learn-react-course/)\\n\\n## Designing with shadcn/ui\\n\\n[shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) is a collection of beautifully designed, accessible components that you can copy and paste into your apps. It's built on top of Radix UI and Tailwind CSS, giving you full control over your components.\\n\\n### Component Libraries & Blocks\\n\\nThese libraries provide pre-built components and blocks that work seamlessly with shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn\\n\\nCurated list of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shadcn.io/awesome)[\\n\\nOrigin UI\\n\\nBeautiful UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://originui.com/)[\\n\\nAnimate UI\\n\\nAnimated components for React\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://animate-ui.com/)[\\n\\nMVP Blocks\\n\\nReady-to-use blocks for MVPs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://blocks.mvp-subha.me/)[\\n\\nSHSF UI\\n\\nModern component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shsfui.com/)[\\n\\nKibo UI\\n\\nAccessible component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.kibo-ui.com/)[\\n\\nReact Bits\\n\\nUseful React components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://reactbits.dev/)[\\n\\nSkiper UI\\n\\nUI components collection\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://skiper-ui.com/)[\\n\\nAceternity UI\\n\\nBeautiful animated components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://ui.aceternity.com/)[\\n\\nMagic UI\\n\\nMagical UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://magicui.design/)[\\n\\nCult UI\\n\\nModern design system\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cult-ui.com/)\\n\\n### Tools & Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools for customizing and extending shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTweakCN\\n\\nCustomize shadcn themes visually\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tweakcn.com/)[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn/ui\\n\\nGitHub collection of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/birobirobiro/awesome-shadcn-ui)\"],[40,\"# JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\\n\\n## Why JavaScript?\\n\\nJavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop software.\\n\\n## Web Dev Speedrun\\n\\nThis is the exact path I took to learn web development. Follow these resources in order to build a good foundation in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Each resource builds on the previous one.\\n\\n[\\n\\n1Responsive Web Design\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - HTML & CSS fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n2Learn HTML\\n\\nCodecademy - Deep dive into HTML\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-html)[\\n\\n3Learn CSS\\n\\nCodecademy - Master CSS styling\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[\\n\\n4Responsive Web Design (2022)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Updated HTML & CSS curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n5JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Core JavaScript concepts\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[\\n\\n6Introduction to JavaScript\\n\\nCodecademy - JavaScript fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/introduction-to-javascript)[\\n\\n7JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures (v8)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Latest JavaScript curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures-v8/)\\n\\n## Node.js\\n\\nNode.js lets you run JavaScript on the server, making you a true full-stack developer. With Node.js, you can build APIs, handle databases, and create complete web applications using the same language you learned for the frontend. Download it from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/en/download).\\n\\n## React\\n\\nOnce you've learned the basics and Node.js, it's time to master React. React is the most popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces and is used by companies like Meta, Netflix, and Airbnb.\\n\\n[\\n\\nReact Official Docs\\n\\nThe best place to learn React from scratch\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://react.dev/learn)[\\n\\nReact Tutorial for Beginners\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Comprehensive React course\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/learn-react-course/)\\n\\n## Designing with shadcn/ui\\n\\n[shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) is a collection of beautifully designed, accessible components that you can copy and paste into your apps. It's built on top of Radix UI and Tailwind CSS, giving you full control over your components.\\n\\n### Component Libraries & Blocks\\n\\nThese libraries provide pre-built components and blocks that work seamlessly with shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn\\n\\nCurated list of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shadcn.io/awesome)[\\n\\nOrigin UI\\n\\nBeautiful UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://originui.com/)[\\n\\nAnimate UI\\n\\nAnimated components for React\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://animate-ui.com/)[\\n\\nMVP Blocks\\n\\nReady-to-use blocks for MVPs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://blocks.mvp-subha.me/)[\\n\\nSHSF UI\\n\\nModern component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shsfui.com/)[\\n\\nKibo UI\\n\\nAccessible component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.kibo-ui.com/)[\\n\\nReact Bits\\n\\nUseful React components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://reactbits.dev/)[\\n\\nSkiper UI\\n\\nUI components collection\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://skiper-ui.com/)[\\n\\nAceternity UI\\n\\nBeautiful animated components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://ui.aceternity.com/)[\\n\\nMagic UI\\n\\nMagical UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://magicui.design/)[\\n\\nCult UI\\n\\nModern design system\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cult-ui.com/)\\n\\n### Tools & Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools for customizing and extending shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTweakCN\\n\\nCustomize shadcn themes visually\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tweakcn.com/)[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn/ui\\n\\nGitHub collection of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/birobirobiro/awesome-shadcn-ui)\"],[13,\"# JavaScript(0)\"],[44,\"# JavaScript(0)\"],[6,\"# Job Board(0)\"],[37,\"# Jobbörse(0)\"],[21,\"# Kotlin(0)\"],[52,\"# Kotlin(0)\"],[1,\"# Latest News\"],[23,\"# Lua(0)\"],[54,\"# Lua(0)\"],[5,\"# Marketplace(0)\"],[36,\"# Marktplatz(0)\"],[32,\"